; A getquote script may print its price line without a date, naming the
; commodity as Ledger passed it to the script: in double quotes, when its
; symbol needs them.  Ledger reads the symbol of such a line as it reads
; that of a dated one, so the price goes to the commodity it asked about,
; not to one whose name includes the quotes, and a space before the line
; is ignored (#3321).

2025/04/29 Buy
    Assets:Broker                   10 "EXV6_DE" @ $48.50
    Assets:Broker                    2 "Fund A" @ $30.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal --market --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-dateless.sh Broker
             $582.00  Assets:Broker
end test
